{"t": 197.022, "n": 119, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the plan to `docs/plans/i144.plan.md` with status `planned`. I didn't run any commands or tests, and I left the commit to the engine.\n\n- **Shape:** It has 9 requirements (R1 to R9) and 2 phases, each of medium weight. There are 6 rows, 2 of them test rows, and they name 6 files. Three verification commands: the full `python -m pytest`, `ruff check src tests` and `mypy`, each run from `plugins/tempergraph/engine`. No row carries a completion mark.\n- **Phase 1, isolation:** The engine ships a pytest plugin, `tempergraph.pytest_plugin`, registered under the `pytest11` entry point. It's an autouse fixture that sets `TEMPERGRAPH_HOME` to a folder of its own and `TEMPERGRAPH_LOOP` to `off`, both through `monkeypatch`. A test that sets the loop mode itself therefore keeps its value. The engine's own `conftest.py` fixture stays as it is. The new test in `test_suite_isolation.py` starts a scratch package from its own folder, in an environment without the home and loop variables. It hashes a seeded `HOME`, machine index included. A control run with the plugin blocked has to change that folder, so the check can fail. The same file also checks the entry point in `pyproject.toml` and that the specs name no workflow.\n- **Phase 2, the verb:** The verb is `stats forget [--check]`, a new action of `stats`. The logic is in a new module, `observe/forget.py`, and `observe_cli.py` wires it in. Tests are in a new `test_central_stats_forget.py`.\n- **Open questions:** I took the hand-off's defaults. Only the month in which the verb runs (UTC) is cleaned. The isolation covers only the home folder and the loop.\n- **Docs to update:** None. Discovery already wrote the spec changes (TST-B7/B8, CST-B17 to B21, the CLI-B8 sentence), and the code now has to match them.\n- **Extra files opened:** The hand-off's reading list was the start. Section 0 of the plan names the four extra files I opened and why: `test_cli.py`, `test_sinks.py`, `test_source_rules.py` and `tempergraph.commands.json`.\n- **doc-refresh copy:** I left `doc-refresh-tgraph`'s own copy of the isolation in place. It isn't part of the criteria.\n\nARTIFACT plan: docs/plans/i144.plan.md\nARTIFACT complexity: simple", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "15c577cf-ac33-4721-bcfa-52500c92caac"}
